[{:adr/consequences "{:positive [\"ISIC 5011 passenger-ferry-operations-coordination genuinely\\n    implemented and fully tested, filling in a pre-existing\\n    :blueprint-tier repo rather than leaving it stale\" \"sail-clearance/weather-hold-override exclusions hardcoded in a\\n    governor check (scope-exclusion-violations), not just README prose\" \"self-trip bug class fixed by construction (action-phrased terms,\\n    disclaimer wording deliberately distinct from the trigger phrases)\\n    + covered by a dedicated cross-op x cross-entity regression test,\\n    not avoided by luck\" \"flag-maritime-safety-concern always-escalate is a two-layer\\n    invariant (governor high-stakes set + phase's permanent absence\\n    from every :auto set, and absence from :writes until phase 3)\" \"effect :propose is a THIRD independent HARD invariant (beyond the\\n    closed op-allowlist and the scope-exclusion check) making the\\n    'this actor never performs a real mutation' design goal\\n    governor-verifiable, not merely conventional\" \"NEW store adopts kotoba-lang/langchain-store (ADR-2607141600)\\n    instead of hand-rolling enc/dec, per skill build-actor's current\\n    guidance\" \"portable .cljc throughout, including tests; clojure -M:lint 0\\n    errors / 0 warnings\"], :negative [\"real persistent store (Datomic/kotoba-server) is a follow-up; tests\\n    use in-memory MemStore + langchain.db in-process DatomicStore,\\n    matching every sibling actor's current maturity\" \"mock-advisor is deterministic, not a real LLM call; Advisor\\n    protocol seam (llm-advisor) is ready for that swap but not wired\\n    live in this ADR\" \"facts catalog seeds only 4 jurisdictions (JPN/USA/GBR/NOR), honestly\\n    reported via ferry.facts/coverage -- not a survey of all ~194\\n    jurisdictions\"]}", :adr/scope-exclusions ["finalizing a sail-clearance decision (clearing a vessel to sail after a reported seaworthiness fault) -- hard, permanent block" "overriding a weather hold -- hard, permanent block" "authorizing departure despite a reported fault -- hard, permanent block" "direct vessel control / real dispatch of any kind -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all; every proposal's :effect is HARD-required to be literally :propose"], :adr/related ["ADR-2607102400" "ADR-2607141600" "ADR-2607011000"], :adr/mirrors "cloud-itonami-isic-5020 (tanker.* module shape, nearest transport-sector sibling) + cloud-itonami-isic-6511 (current-gen langchain-store + portable .cljc test convention, reference adopter)", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "adr-2629500000-cloud-itonami-isic-5011-sea-passenger-transport-coverage", :adr/context "ISIC Rev.5 5011 = sea and coastal passenger water transport. Live\n  registry.edn :name for \"5011\" independently verified fresh (cloned\n  kotoba-lang/industry read-only): \"Sea and coastal passenger water\n  transport\", exact match. Unlike most cloud-itonami-isic-* targets in\n  this fleet, this was NOT a 404 target -- cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-\n  isic-5011 already existed as a legitimate :blueprint-tier scaffold,\n  published by ADR-2607102400 (created+pushed 2026-07-09) with\n  boilerplate docs (CODE_OF_CONDUCT/\n  CONTRIBUTING/GOVERNANCE/LICENSE/README/SECURITY/blueprint.edn/docs)\n  but no deps.edn/src/test. blueprint.edn already declared\n  :itonami.blueprint/governor :maritime-safety-governor and README\n  already named a 'Ferry Operations Advisor -> Maritime Safety\n  Governor' contract -- confirmed via `gh api\n  repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5011` before starting, per\n  this task's premise-verification requirement. This ADR records\n  filling that scaffold in, not creating a fresh repo.\n  cloud-itonami-isic-4911 (passenger rail), the originally suggested\n  mirror target, was itself still :blueprint-tier (being built\n  concurrently by a sibling agent in this same batch), so\n  cloud-itonami-isic-5020 (water freight/tanker, :implemented) and\n  cloud-itonami-isic-6511 (life insurance, :implemented, pushed\n  2026-07-14, the kotoba-lang/langchain-store reference adopter) were\n  used as the mirrored references instead. Passenger ferry service has\n  a direct passenger-safety dimension (maritime) -- per this batch's\n  Wave 2 (coordination/logistics) guardrail, the closed op allowlist\n  must never include an op that directly finalizes a maritime-safety-\n  authority decision; any 'flag a concern' op always escalates, never\n  auto-commit-eligible.", :adr/adr-id "2629500000", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/body "# ADR-2629500000: cloud-itonami ISIC 5011 (Sea and coastal passenger water transport) coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted. `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5011` promoted from\n`:blueprint` to `:implemented` in the `kotoba-lang/industry` registry.\n\n## Context\n\n`kotoba-lang/industry`'s registry entry `{:id \"5011\" ...}` resolves to\n`:name \"Sea and coastal passenger water transport\"`\n(`:business-id \"cloud-itonami-5011\"`,\n`:repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5011\"`,\nverified against the live registry before starting this work).\n\nUnlike most `cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors built in this fleet's recent\nbatches, `cloud-itonami-isic-5011` was NOT a fresh 404 target: the\nGitHub repository already existed as a legitimate `:blueprint`-tier\nscaffold, published by `ADR-2607102400` (the THIRTEENTH \"author a new\nblueprint from `:spec` tier\" build, closing out a three-mode air/rail/\nwater transport family alongside `cloud-itonami-isic-5110` and\n`cloud-itonami-isic-4911`) from an earlier bulk-scaffolding pass\n(created and pushed 2026-07-09, boilerplate docs -- `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`\n/ `CONTRIBUTING.md` / `GOVERNANCE.md` / `LICENSE` / `README.edn` /\n`SECURITY.md` / `blueprint.edn` / `docs/business-model.md` /\n`docs/operator-guide.md` -- with no `deps.edn`, `src`, or `test`, per\nthat ADR's own Decision 1 explicitly reserving those for \"a future\n`:blueprint`->`:implemented` promotion pass\").\n`blueprint.edn` already declared\n`:itonami.blueprint/governor :maritime-safety-governor` and the\n`README.edn` already named a \"Ferry Operations Advisor -> Maritime\nSafety Governor\" core contract, `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :logistics]` and\n`:optional-technologies [:optimization]` (all already correct, no\nfield-sync fix needed). This ADR records filling that scaffold in with\na real, tested implementation -- not creating the repository fresh.\n\nThe nearest already-`:implemented` transport-sector sibling at the time\nof this build was `cloud-itonami-isic-5020` (water freight transport /\ntanker) -- `cloud-itonami-isic-4911` (passenger rail, the originally\nsuggested mirror target) was itself still `:blueprint`-tier, being\nbuilt concurrently by a sibling agent in this same fleet batch, so\n`cloud-itonami-isic-5020` and the current-generation\n`cloud-itonami-isic-6511` (life insurance, the `kotoba-lang/langchain-\nstore` reference adopter, pushed 2026-07-14) were used as the mirrored\nreferences instead.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: passenger-ferry OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor, not maritime-safety authority\n\nPer this task's explicit domain design, `cloud-itonami-isic-5011` is\nscoped as an operations-coordination actor, deliberately narrower than\n`cloud-itonami-isic-5020`'s dispatch/discharge-drafting tanker actor:\nevery proposal's `:effect` is HARD-required to be the literal keyword\n`:propose` (`ferry.governor/effect-not-propose-violations`), and there\nis no domain-specific mutation-effect keyword. Four governed ops, a\nclosed allowlist enforced independently at the governor layer\n(`ferry.governor/op-not-allowed-violations`), all effect `:propose`:\n`:log-voyage-record`, `:schedule-sailing-operation`, `:flag-maritime-\nsafety-concern`, `:coordinate-maintenance`.\n\n### Decision 2: the scope-exclusion self-trip bug class, fixed by construction\n\nThis fleet has repeatedly hit and independently fixed the SAME bug\nclass across multiple sibling actors: a governor's scope-exclusion term\nlist phrased as a bare noun (e.g. \"safety\", \"clearance\", \"weather-\nhold\") accidentally matches inside the actor's own DEFAULT advisor\nrationale/disclaimer text, because an honest disclaimer explaining what\nthe actor does NOT do necessarily uses the bare noun it is disclaiming\n-- causing the actor to self-block on its own happy path.\n\nFix applied here: `ferry.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases` (in\n`cloud-itonami-isic-5011`'s own repo) is a set of full FINALIZATION/\nEXECUTION ACTIONS (\"finalize the sail-clearance override\", \"override\nthe weather-hold\", etc.), never a bare noun, and `ferry.ferryadvisor`'s\nown rationale/disclaimer text is written in different words than any of\nthose phrases (attributing final departure-clearance judgment to \"the\nvessel master and the maritime-safety authority\" rather than restating\nwhat the actor does not do). `test/ferry/scope_exclusion_test.cljc` is\na dedicated regression test sweeping every op x every demo sailing\n(including a fault-reported + weather-hold-active one) through the\nDEFAULT mock advisor and asserting none of the resulting proposals trip\n`:scope-exclusion-sail-clearance`; a separate direct-unit test file\n(`test/ferry/governor_test.cljc`) proves the check is not vacuous.\n\n### Decision 3: Wave 2 (coordination/logistics) maritime-safety invariant\n\nPer this fleet batch's Wave 2 policy for passenger-safety-adjacent\ncoordination actors: the closed op-allowlist never includes an op that\ndirectly finalizes a maritime-safety-authority decision (clearing a\nvessel to sail after a reported fault, overriding a weather hold) --\nthese are always either a hard permanent block (the scope-exclusion\ncheck, Decision 2) or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible.\n`:flag-maritime-safety-concern` (the \"flag a concern\" op) always\nescalates to human sign-off via TWO independent layers\n(`ferry.governor/high-stakes` AND `ferry.phase` never putting it in any\nphase's `:auto` set) and is never in any phase's `:auto` set, including\nphase 3.\n\n### Decision 4: self-contained domain logic, `langchain-store` store seam\n\nLike `cloud-itonami-isic-5020`, no `kotoba-lang/maritime` capability\nlibrary exists to delegate passenger-vessel safety validation to.\n`ferry.registry/imo-number-valid?` honestly reapplies `cloud-itonami-\nisic-5020`'s own reapplication of the SOLAS / IMO resolution A.600(15)\nseven-digit check-digit scheme (applies to every SOLAS-class ship,\nincluding passenger vessels, not only tankers). Because this is a NEW\nstore as of 2026-07, it adopts `kotoba-lang/langchain-store`\n(ADR-2607141600) as its `DatomicStore` field-spec entity-store seam\n(the `cloud-itonami-isic-6511` `underwriting.store` pattern) rather than\nhand-rolling the `enc`/`dec*` + schema/pull boilerplate `cloud-itonami-\nisic-5020` (which predates that library) hand-rolls.\n\n### Decision 5: portable `.cljc` throughout (cljs-first mandate)\n\nPer this workspace's CLAUDE.md runtime priority (`kotoba wasm >\nclojurewasm > ClojureScript > nbb`, JVM/bb last resort) and its explicit\n\"no JVM-only interop\" instruction for this build, ALL source AND test\nfiles are `.cljc` (not `.clj`), including a `ferry.portable-cljs-test-\nrunner` + `:cljs` deps.edn alias -- a deliberate departure from\n`cloud-itonami-isic-5020`'s `.clj`-only test suite, which predates that\nmandate, and a mirror of `cloud-itonami-isic-6511`'s current-generation\nconvention.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:dev:test` in the built repo: `Ran 46 tests containing 272\n  assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.` (raw output captured; re-verified\n  again after a fresh clone post-merge).\n- `clojure -M:lint`: 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- `clojure -M:dev:run`: demo walks the happy paths (log -> schedule ->\n  flag-concern -> coordinate-maintenance, all via escalate/approve/\n  commit except the auto-committing voyage-record log) plus every\n  HARD-hold scenario (no spec-basis, invalid IMO, certification\n  incomplete on all three non-logging ops, already scheduled) and a\n  low-confidence-but-governor-clean escalation (fault-reported +\n  weather-hold-active), end-to-end, exit 0.\n- Registry: `kotoba-lang/industry`'s `{:id \"5011\" ...}` entry, which had\n  no `:maturity` key (resolved to `:blueprint` via the `:repo`-present\n  fallback in `kotoba.industry/maturity-of`), now has `:maturity\n  :implemented` added explicitly (commit\n  `23db6561e48ed605f979465aee6f16f0eadaccf9`). `:repo` and\n  `:business-id` were already correct (no change needed).\n- `test/kotoba/industry_test.clj` (a very hot contention file, re-fetched\n  fresh multiple times over the course of this edit as concurrent\n  sibling agents landed several other promotions in the same window)\n  got a dedicated corroboration block for 5011 (final content, commit\n  `dbdcec1107af99aad51d3b0a037f1f7c638ad79d`). Honesty note: an\n  intermediate PUT attempt (commit `83a1aedbc040f09599e70899a2cf8ea0b96e82f0`)\n  accidentally sent EMPTY content due to a local `base64` CLI-argument\n  error (BSD `base64` on macOS silently no-ops without `-i`), briefly\n  zeroing the shared file; caught immediately by this session's\n  standing post-PUT re-fetch-and-diff verification and corrected within\n  the same turn, then independently re-verified via a brand-new fresh\n  clone. See the paired `.edn`'s `:incident-note` for the full account.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Sea and coastal passenger water transport (ISIC 5011) actor on the\n  same governed-actor architecture as the rest of the cloud-itonami\n  fleet, filling in a pre-existing `:blueprint`-tier repo rather than\n  scaffolding a new one.\n- The scope-exclusion self-trip bug class now has a THIRD (at least)\n  independent fix-and-regression-test instance in this fleet, plus a\n  fleet-wide-legible design record (this ADR + the child repo's own\n  `docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`) of the fix pattern (full action\n  phrases, not bare nouns, plus a dedicated cross-op x cross-entity\n  sweep test) for future actors in maritime-safety-adjacent or other\n  authority-adjacent domains to follow.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607102400-cloud-itonami-passengerferry-5011-blueprint.edn`\n  (the originating blueprint-publication ADR this build promotes from)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5011/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (child-repo\n  architecture ADR, full design record)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-6511/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md`\n  (current-generation governed-actor architecture +\n  `kotoba-lang/langchain-store` reference adopter this build follows)\n- `cloud-itonami-isic-5020/docs/adr/0001-architecture.md` (nearest\n  transport-sector sibling; contrast: marine CARGO not passenger, no\n  `:effect :propose` constant, pre-`langchain-store`, `.clj` tests)\n- ADR-2607141600 (`kotoba-lang/langchain-store` store-seam\n  commonalization)\n- IMO resolution A.600(15): IMO Ship Identification Number Scheme", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki (agent-executed, standing authorization)"], :adr/decision "Fill in the pre-existing cloud-itonami-isic-5011 :blueprint scaffold\n  with a real, tested FerryOperationsAdvisor + Maritime Safety Governor\n  actor, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-5020's tanker.* module shape as\n  ferry.*:\n  - Store (ferry.store): Store protocol + MemStore + DatomicStore, the\n    latter a kotoba-lang/langchain-store field-spec entity-store\n    adopter (ADR-2607141600, NOT hand-rolled enc/dec -- this is a NEW\n    store as of 2026-07). sailing entity (vessel-imo/jurisdiction/\n    certification-verified?/certification-record-id/seaworthiness-\n    fault-reported?/weather-hold-active?/scheduled?/maintenance-\n    coordinated?), append-only ledger + schedule/concern/maintenance\n    history, MemStore<->DatomicStore contract parity proven.\n  - Facts (ferry.facts): per-jurisdiction passenger-vessel safety-\n    certification catalog (JPN/USA/GBR/NOR), real citations (MLIT/\n    USCG/MCA/NMA, SOLAS Chapter III life-saving appliances), honest\n    coverage reporting -- deliberately SEPARATE regime from\n    cloud-itonami-isic-5020's cargo-vessel (SOLAS Chapter II-2) facts.\n  - Registry (ferry.registry): draft record construction (sailing-\n    schedule/concern-filing/maintenance-coordination, all unsigned\n    drafts) + imo-number-valid? (honest reapplication of\n    cloud-itonami-isic-5020's SOLAS/IMO A.600(15) 7-digit check-digit\n    scheme -- applies to every SOLAS-class ship, not only tankers).\n  - Advisor (ferry.ferryadvisor): Advisor protocol + mock-advisor +\n    llm-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose -- log-voyage-record,\n    schedule-sailing-operation, flag-maritime-safety-concern,\n    coordinate-maintenance.\n  - Governor (ferry.governor, the Maritime Safety Governor): 7 named\n    HARD checks in priority order (op-not-allowed, effect-not-propose,\n    scope-exclusion-sail-clearance [permanent], certification-\n    incomplete, imo-number-invalid, no-spec-basis, already-scheduled)\n    + high-stakes gate #{:flag-maritime-safety-concern} + confidence\n    floor 0.6.\n  - Phase (ferry.phase): 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-voyage-record only,\n    approval; phase2 += schedule-sailing-operation, approval; phase3\n    writes all 4 ops but auto-commits ONLY log-voyage-record;\n    flag-maritime-safety-concern never auto, any phase, AND not\n    writable until phase 3).\n  - Operation (ferry.operation): real langgraph-clj StateGraph\n    (intake->advise->govern->decide->commit|hold|request-approval),\n    interrupt-before #{:request-approval}, NOT a stub -- mirrors\n    tanker.operation/underwriting.operation exactly. commit-record\n    dispatch keyed on the request's :op (not the proposal's :effect,\n    which is a constant :propose by design) -- documented explicitly\n    as a deliberate deviation from the mirrored siblings.\n  - Sim (ferry.sim): clojure -M:dev:run demo, happy paths + always-\n    escalate flow + a low-confidence-but-clean escalation + every\n    HARD-hold scenario.\n  - Tests, all .cljc (not .clj, per this workspace's cljs-first\n    mandate): facts_test, registry_test, phase_test, governor_test\n    (direct unit tests of op-not-allowed/effect-not-propose/scope-\n    exclusion, incl. the mandatory self-trip regression date),\n    governor_contract_test (full-graph flows), store_contract_test,\n    scope_exclusion_test (the dedicated CRITICAL regression), plus a\n    portable-cljs-test-runner + :cljs deps.edn alias mirroring\n    cloud-itonami-isic-6511's current-generation convention.\n  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later.\n    Existing boilerplate docs (README/GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/\n    SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT/blueprint.edn/docs/business-model.md/\n    docs/operator-guide.md) were KEPT, not recreated; README.edn was\n    extended (not replaced) with R0/Run/Layout/Maturity sections; a\n    docs/adr/0001-architecture.md child-repo ADR was added.", :adr/date "2026-07-16", :db/id -1, :adr/self-trip-fix "Known bug class this fleet has repeatedly hit and independently fixed\n  across multiple sibling actors: a governor's scope-exclusion term list\n  phrased as a bare noun (e.g. 'safety', 'clearance', 'weather-hold')\n  accidentally matches inside the mock advisor's own DEFAULT\n  rationale/disclaimer text for a legitimate, allowed proposal --\n  especially acute here since :schedule-sailing-operation's own\n  rationale, when the sailing has a reported fault or active weather\n  hold, necessarily discusses those exact conditions, and\n  :flag-maritime-safety-concern's entire purpose is to surface them.\n  Fix: ferry.governor/scope-exclusion-phrases is phrased as full\n  finalization/execution ACTIONS ('finalize the sail-clearance\n  override', 'override the weather-hold', 'clear the vessel to sail\n  despite the fault', 'authorize departure despite the reported\n  fault'), never a bare noun -- and ferry.ferryadvisor's own\n  rationale/disclaimer text is written in DIFFERENT words than any of\n  those phrases (attributing final departure-clearance judgment to\n  'the vessel master and the maritime-safety authority' rather than\n  restating what the actor itself does not do, so no negation of the\n  exact trigger phrase appears either). Verified via a dedicated\n  regression test, default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-\n  scope-exclusion in test/ferry/scope_exclusion_test.cljc, sweeping\n  every op (:log-voyage-record/:schedule-sailing-operation/\n  :flag-maritime-safety-concern/:coordinate-maintenance) x every demo\n  sailing (including sail-6, the fault-reported + weather-hold-active\n  one) through the DEFAULT mock advisor and asserting none of the\n  resulting proposals trip :scope-exclusion-sail-clearance. A separate\n  direct-unit-test file, test/ferry/governor_test.cljc, proves the\n  check is not vacuous: a hand-crafted proposal containing each phrase\n  verbatim IS hard-blocked.", :adr/verification "{:lint-status \"0 errors, 0 warnings (clojure -M:lint)\", :registry-update \"kotoba-lang/industry: 5011 had no :maturity key (resolved to :blueprint via the :repo-present fallback) -> :maturity :implemented added explicitly via an exact-text in-place edit of only the {:id \\\"5011\\\" ...} block (Contents-API single-file PUT, sha-checked, prefix/suffix-scan-verified single contiguous changed region, commit 23db6561e48ed605f979465aee6f16f0eadaccf9). :repo/:business-id/:required-technologies/:optional-technologies were already correct (no change needed). test/kotoba/industry_test.clj (a VERY hot contention file, re-fetched fresh 3 times over the course of this edit as concurrent sibling agents landed 5+ other promotions in the same window) got a new dedicated corroboration block for 5011 plus a tail-count comment (commit dbdcec1107af99aad51d3b0a037f1f7c638ad79d, the FINAL landed content -- see :incident-note below for an intermediate corrective PUT to this same commit path).\", :assertion-count 272, :test-status \"0 failures, 0 errors -- clojure -M:dev:test run at push time AND independently re-run from a brand-new fresh clone post-merge, identical result\", :test-count 46, :commit \"a934087697cdcf39448b8a7a31e6b6cc6ddafca1\", :incident-note \"Honesty note (no failure hidden): the FIRST attempt to PUT the corrected industry_test.clj (commit 83a1aedbc040f09599e70899a2cf8ea0b96e82f0) accidentally sent EMPTY content -- a local `base64 <file>` invocation silently failed on this macOS's BSD base64 (which requires `-i <file>`, not a bare filename argument) and the script proceeded to PUT the resulting empty output without an explicit non-empty-content guard. This zeroed the live shared test file for well under a minute. Caught immediately by an unconditional post-PUT re-fetch-and-diff verification (this session's own standing practice, not a one-off), and corrected within the same turn by a second Contents-API PUT (commit dbdcec1107af99aad51d3b0a037f1f7c638ad79d) restoring the exact intended content, re-verified byte-for-byte identical to the locally-tested version afterward, then re-verified again via a brand-new fresh clone (`clojure -M:test`: 15 tests / 1061 assertions, 0 failures/0 errors; `clojure -M:lint`: 0 errors/0 warnings; no mojibake; 5011 entry and sample entries 3512/5020/5221 all intact). No other concurrent sibling PUT raced into the empty window. Lesson for future agents: always pass an explicit `-i <file> -o <file>` (or pipe via stdin) to `base64` on macOS, and always verify a PUT payload's `content` field is non-empty (e.g. assert base64 length > some floor) before sending, not only after.\", :demo-run \"clojure -M:dev:run end-to-end, exit 0: log-voyage-record auto-commits at phase 3; schedule-sailing-operation/coordinate-maintenance escalate then commit after approval; flag-maritime-safety-concern ALWAYS escalates then commits after approval; a fault-reported+weather-hold-active sailing's schedule proposal escalates on low confidence (not a hard hold) and still commits after human approval, WITHOUT self-tripping the scope-exclusion check; no-spec-basis / invalid-IMO / certification-incomplete (on all 3 non-logging ops) / already-scheduled all HARD-hold as designed, no interrupt\", :repo \"https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5011\"}", :adr/title "cloud-itonami ISIC 5011 (sea and coastal passenger water transport) FerryOperationsAdvisor + Maritime Safety Governor actor", :adr/source-format "edn"}]